          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: The observation of a group of orange balls (around twenty according to the witness), for several minutes, at 23:53 on a Friday night, suggests a release of Thai lanterns following a festival. The witness observes the balls almost stationary, very slightly moving to the left as they weaken: the lanterns, pushed by the wind, move away from the witness, slightly towards the West. Meteociel indicates a light west or northwest wind of 13 to 19 km/h at Roissy: Weather. No other testimony will be collected. This case is classified as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
